<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Bentley, Gerhardt & Bates (2008) PLoS Comput. Biol., Hellström et al. (2007) Nature & Jakobsson et al. (2010) Nat. Cell Biol. VEGF-VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 tip/stalk salt-and-pepper lateral inhibition and angiogenic sprouting — MorphoEval overall 51.9/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 (v1) baseline evaluation of `2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py` (weighted score: 53.0/100). The Pass 1 baseline integrates only an isolated two-cell Dll4-Notch1 ODE at two trans-Notch gains (k_t = 1.0 and 0.0) without solving the multicellular M=16 endothelial vessel wall coupled VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 + 2D filopodial angiogenic sprout elongation network across the 5 canonical biological regimes (Physiological VEGF gradient salt-and-pepper, High uniform VEGF synchronous oscillations, DAPT Notch blockade all-tip hypersprouting, Dll4+/- haploinsufficiency, and Vegfr2+/- mosaic chimeric tip competition Jakobsson et al. 2010), omits VEGFR1/sFlt1 decoy sequestration and the 8-point Notch trans-gain sweep, and does not segment the vendored Homo sapiens HUVEC angiogenic sprouting vascular plexus micrograph. Overall 51.9/100 (faithfulness 49.1, reproducibility 58.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 54, Morphological realism / specimen match 44, Parameter expressivity 49, Morphometric validation 51, Source and data traceability 68, Code-to-model traceability 55, Reproducibility package 53. Output judged: docs/media/vascular_angiogenesis_notch_comparison.png: rendered output of 2021-ibrahim-vascular-angiogenesis-notch.py at 8871db0, image/png, 81701 B, 1365×572 px, artifact_sha256 752052d83f74a51a8a136bd0628b68dd31a9e00f6acf6e2876d07385b72d3982 (sha256 752052d83f74a51a8a136bd0628b68dd31a9e00f6acf6e2876d07385b72d3982), spec_fingerprint 75ad27375139b901d6c87702d5f02c739a8e698db79579ceae73bdab1d021c1b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 75ad27375139b901d6c87702d5f02c739a8e698db79579ceae73bdab1d021c1b; artifact_sha256: 752052d83f74a51a8a136bd0628b68dd31a9e00f6acf6e2876d07385b72d3982; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/huvec_angiogenic_sprouting_plexus_specimen.jpg=9bf4f3e2692bd2ac..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/paper_citations.bib=a96e44f99de8a756..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/scout_manifest.json=2b97b38c418e4c44..., datasets/vascular_angiogenesis_notch/vascular_angiogenesis_notch_reference.json=8821743569ceaf2e...}." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Implement the coupled multicellular M=16 Bentley-Gerhardt-Bates VEGFR2-Dll4-Notch1 lateral-inhibition ODE network + 2D filopodial angiogenic sprout elongation solver with soluble VEGFR1 (sFlt1) decoy sequestration.",
        "remediation needed: Segment the vendored Homo sapiens HUVEC angiogenic sprouting vascular network micrograph (`huvec_angiogenic_sprouting_plexus_specimen.jpg`, CC BY 4.0) to extract vascular plexus area density, branch junctions, and sprouting tip count, backed by runtime SHA-256 verification and an 8-suite `--self-test`.",
        "remediation needed: Simulate all 5 canonical angiogenic regimes (Physiological VEGF gradient salt-and-pepper, High uniform VEGF synchronous oscillations, DAPT Notch blockade hypersprouting, Dll4+/- haploinsufficiency, and Vegfr2+/- mosaic chimeric tip competition Jakobsson et al. 2010) plus an 8-point Notch trans-activation gain sweep." ;
    pk:hasScore 5.19e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

